  "notes": "No motif on the Prophet ﷺ; no key on the negated «خزائن الله». A lamp for 50:26 (the one who sees: the believer), night and day for 52:6. 51:9-15 not glossed (no excerpt keeps «ليس… ولا» without repeating the verse). 52:22-25 keeps Al-Muyassar's condition «فإن أبعدتهم». No ranking of the Companions. STAGING v4: 50 (the Prophet's own statement) stays ambient; mood light -> night_sky (no rays over his first-person words), a lamp plate on 50:26 (the one who sees, the believer: guidance), not light. 51-52: three believers sit at home at dusk (not a mosque hall, so nothing suggests his gathering) and read the Quran on 51:2 (Al-Muyassar: this Quran is a warning), lower their heads on 51:5 (those who fear the Gathering, nothing of it drawn), raise their hands on 52:4 (both tafsirs: they call on and worship their Lord morning and evening; a night-and-day plate on 52:6); they stay in place for the whole chapter, nobody leaves or turns (the counterfactual driving away is never shown); As-Sa'di tells the occasion (the chiefs asking him to send the poor away) but it is deliberately not staged: no chiefs or rich men, no lone man, no empty seat; no pan on the words addressed to the Prophet (camera close or wide only), a wide shot and a two-paths plate on 52:22 so the camera does not hold on the believers for the warning"
